      "b": "degas",
      "kind": "Japanese prints in common with",
      "word": "Japanese",
      "note": "Both were collecting and studying Japanese prints in the 1860s, and both took the same lesson: the off-centre subject, the cropped edge, the flat interval of empty ground."
