      "kind": "the two poles of the Dutch century",
      "word": "Dutch",
      "note": "The two poles of the Dutch century: Rembrandt made some three hundred paintings, Vermeer perhaps thirty-five. One painted the whole world in brown light; the other painted one corner of one room and got everything into it."
