      "kind": "court painter to",
      "word": "Napoleon",
      "note": "David painted the coronation in Notre-Dame — twenty feet by thirty — and put Napoleon’s mother in the gallery watching, though she had refused to attend. He became First Painter to the Emperor and followed him into exile."
